on pavement versus trails?

02:20:29.053 --> 02:20:31.256
- Oh, I love trails.

02:20:31.256 --> 02:20:33.057
I mean, why did I
move to the Valley?

02:20:33.057 --> 02:20:36.027 align:start size:88% position:13%
Because I wanted to
soak up all the trails.

02:20:36.027 --> 02:20:37.829
- 818 baby.
- I love it.

02:20:37.829 --> 02:20:42.767
So I try to run soft
for all easy runs.

02:20:44.936 --> 02:20:48.907
I end up needing to go
on a track or on roads

02:20:48.907 --> 02:20:52.811 align:start position:0%
for some of these workouts
because I have to train my body

02:20:54.145 --> 02:20:56.614
to handle certain services,

02:20:56.614 --> 02:21:00.552
but I'm on soft and on
trails as much as I can.

02:21:00.552 --> 02:21:01.886
And I love it.

02:21:03.655 --> 02:21:07.392
I love how undiscovered the
trails of LA seemed to be.

02:21:07.392 --> 02:21:09.127
I know that there are
people running here

02:21:09.127 --> 02:21:12.163 align:start position:0%
but it's not something that
people talk about in the world.

02:21:12.163 --> 02:21:16.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
- It's crazy to me
because the trail system,

02:21:18.870 --> 02:21:22.006 align:start size:97% position:3%
the amount of like untouched
land in Los Angeles

02:21:22.006 --> 02:21:23.475
is pretty extraordinary,

02:21:23.475 --> 02:21:27.712
but it's kind of blind
to the casual observer

02:21:27.712 --> 02:21:29.214 align:start size:81% position:19%
who's just driving
on the freeway.

02:21:29.214 --> 02:21:31.282
Like you see the
hills over there,

02:21:31.282 --> 02:21:33.985
but then when you're
actually up there,

02:21:33.985 --> 02:21:36.187
yeah, there's a few runners
and now with gravel bikes,

02:21:36.187 --> 02:21:37.489
there's more people on bikes,

02:21:37.489 --> 02:21:40.425
but overall, there's
barely anybody up there

02:21:40.425 --> 02:21:42.560
and you could be up
in Topanga State Park

02:21:42.560 --> 02:21:45.630
and it's like natural land
for as far as you can see

02:21:45.630 --> 02:21:47.432
and you're right in the
middle of Los Angeles.

02:21:47.432 --> 02:21:50.335 align:start size:84% position:16%
It makes Central Park
look like a speck

02:21:50.335 --> 02:21:51.903 align:start size:81% position:19%
compared to what's
available here.

02:21:51.903 --> 02:21:54.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when you're up there-
- Quote him, okay.

02:21:54.138 --> 02:21:56.274
I said quote him.
(both laughing)

02:21:56.274 --> 02:21:57.575
- I mean, when you're
up there you're like,

02:21:57.575 --> 02:21:59.244
why isn't everybody up here?

02:21:59.244 --> 02:22:00.612
Like, there's no...

02:22:00.612 --> 02:22:04.782 align:start size:97% position:3%
For such a densely
populated urban metropolis,

02:22:04.782 --> 02:22:07.085
I'll see like three
people, you know,

02:22:07.085 --> 02:22:09.754
in like over a course
of multiple hours.

02:22:09.754 --> 02:22:12.156 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, and I feel
that the greatest gift

02:22:12.156 --> 02:22:13.625
that people have given me here

02:22:13.625 --> 02:22:16.394 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that you could give
someone if you're interested

02:22:16.394 --> 02:22:20.131 align:start position:0%
in running in trails or walking
is to show them a trail.

02:22:23.334 --> 02:22:25.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you don't know
that they're there, right?

02:22:25.303 --> 02:22:28.139 align:start size:88% position:13%
- And you know, I'll
call myself out on that.

02:22:28.139 --> 02:22:29.541
Like I lived here for years

02:22:29.541 --> 02:22:32.110 align:start size:84% position:16%
before I ever went and
explored any of it.

02:22:32.110 --> 02:22:34.913 align:start position:0%
And then when I did, I was
like, oh my God, I had no idea.

02:22:34.913 --> 02:22:36.214
- Yeah, yeah.

02:22:36.214 --> 02:22:38.650
So, I'm loving it.

02:22:38.650 --> 02:22:42.987 align:start size:84% position:16%
I feel it's a
forever place for me.

02:22:42.987 --> 02:22:47.892 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I've met friends
through the trail system

02:22:47.892 --> 02:22:50.695 align:start size:88% position:13%
like while on the
trail I've met friends,

02:22:52.163 --> 02:22:56.067
and it's just like
a treasure trove.

02:22:56.067 --> 02:23:00.405
I love the early mornings and
in the sunsets are the best

02:23:01.573 --> 02:23:06.377
and it is a good
way to get to know

02:23:09.380 --> 02:23:11.849
a city is on the trails I think.

02:23:13.217 --> 02:23:14.819
- Well, we got to end
this shortly here.

02:23:14.819 --> 02:23:17.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't wanna be too
indulgent with your time,

02:23:17.755 --> 02:23:19.691
but before I let you go,

02:23:19.691 --> 02:23:23.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think a good way to
end it is with just a few

02:23:24.796 --> 02:23:28.266
sort of bravey thoughts for
the person who's listening,

02:23:28.266 --> 02:23:30.668
who's maybe feeling
stuck or struggling

02:23:30.668 --> 02:23:34.639
or feels like they're not
entitled to have a dream

02:23:34.639 --> 02:23:38.409
or that aspirational life
that they seek, you know,

02:23:38.409 --> 02:23:41.379
just feels too inaccessible.

02:23:41.379 --> 02:23:44.849 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, to you
bravey listening in,

02:23:44.849 --> 02:23:48.553 align:start size:97% position:3%
I take your dream seriously,
even if you do not.

02:23:48.553 --> 02:23:53.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you're allowed to take
